# Feature-first folder structure

All new React app code lives under `src/react-app/` using **features**, not scattered `client/`, `lib/auth`, or root-level UI folders.

## Target tree

```
src/react-app/
  app/                          # Bootstrap only: router, providers, route-guards
  routes/                       # Thin route files — wire locale/params, render feature pages
  features/
    <feature>/                  # auth | dashboard | account | …
      components/               # UI owned by this feature
      hooks/
      services/                 # client-side orchestration
      requests/                 # API calls
      schemas/                  # zod / validation
      lib/                      # helpers private to this feature
      index.ts                  # public exports — other code imports from here
  shared/                       # Cross-feature: http, i18n, routing, query, auth session
  ui/                           # App-wide shells & Astryx templates (layout, login-card, settings)
  lib/                          # Non-UI infra only: assets, config, contracts, platform, providers, types
    astryx/                     # Thin Astryx adapters (toast, breadcrumbs, form-dialog)
```

Worker code stays in `src/worker/` (not under `features/`).

## Placement rules

| What | Where | Not here |
|------|--------|----------|
| Login form, register, 2FA UI | `features/auth/` | `lib/auth/`, `lib/common/` |
| Dashboard, settings page, charts | `features/dashboard/` | `lib/ui/` (except layout shell) |
| Account API + hooks | `features/account/` | mixed into dashboard without reason |
| Astryx template scaffold | `ui/<template>/` | repo root, `login-card/` at react-app root |
| Layout shell (side nav) | `ui/shell-side-nav/` | `features/dashboard/components/` |
| Toast, AppBreadcrumbs | `lib/astryx/` | feature folders |
| HTTP client, i18n messages | `shared/` | inside a single feature |
| Env, cookies, route guards | `lib/platform/` (cookies, HTTP) + `shared/routing/guards` + `app/` | feature components |

## File rules

1. **One feature = one folder** under `features/<name>/`. No top-level `components/` dump.
2. **`routes/` stays thin** — no business logic; import from `features/<name>`.
3. **Cross-feature imports** — only from `features/<other>/index.ts`, never deep paths into another feature.
4. **No duplicate modules** — one canonical path (e.g. one login-card under `ui/login-card/`).
5. **Do not add** to legacy paths: `client/features/`, `lib/components/`, `lib/common/`, `lib/auth/` (migrate when editing those files).
6. **New Astryx template** — `pnpm exec astryx template <name> ./src/react-app/ui/<name> -f`; production code in same folder, exclude `page.tsx` from tsconfig if reference-only.

## Imports (current → target)

```tsx
// ✅ Feature-internal
import { LoginForm } from '@/features/auth/components/login-form';

// ✅ Other feature — public API
import { DashboardShell } from '@/features/dashboard';

// ✅ Shared / infra
import { api } from '@/shared/http/client';
import { ToastProvider } from '@tanlabs/astryx';

// ❌ Deep cross-feature
import { useRegisterForm } from '@/features/auth/hooks/use-register-form'; // from dashboard

// ❌ Legacy / duplicate roots
import { AuthLayout } from '@/features/auth'; // use public API from index.ts
```

`@/` → `src/react-app`. Prefer `@/features/*`, `@/shared/*`, `@/ui/*` over `@tanlabs/ui/*`.

## Adding a feature

```
features/billing/
  components/billing-page.tsx
  hooks/use-billing.ts
  requests/billing.requests.ts
  index.ts          # export { BillingPage } from './components/billing-page'
routes/billing.tsx  # <BillingPage lang={...} />
```
